SET ECHO OFF
* ============================================================
* MEMO_X64_REOPEN_CANARY_20260513.DTS
*
* Purpose:
*   Isolate the active x64 memo reopen/update bug without polluting the
*   integrated x64 regression harness.
*
* STATUS UPDATE 2026-08-11: both reds below were re-measured GREEN on the
* RAM-VFS path by memo_ram_hello.dts (H_T2 reopen readback, H_T3 update
* after reopen -- registered as REGRESSION RUN MEMO_RAM_HELLO). The fix
* most plausibly rode the memo_auto sidecar lifecycle work. THIS canary
* runs the DISK path and has NOT been rerun since 2026-05-13: the
* expectations below are three months stale. Next runner: rerun this
* script; if green, repoint or retire it with the green recorded
* (IDXSTALE precedent -- the subject moved, the test was not wrong).
*
* Known-red behavior as originally observed 2026-05-13 (now historical):
*   - CREATE X64 ... NOTES M succeeds.
*   - Initial REPLACE NOTES WITH "first x64 memo" appears correct before CLOSE.
*   - After CLOSE / USE MEMO_X64, TUP shows NOTES as memo reference value "1"
*     instead of "first x64 memo".
*   - Later REPLACE NOTES reports: REPLACE: memo backend not attached.
*
* Expected eventual green behavior:
*   - Reopen should reattach the x64 memo backend.
*   - TUP / TUPLE NOTES should read back memo text.
*   - REPLACE NOTES should update, clear, and reinsert memo text after reopen.
*
* Safety:
*   - Destructive only to the MEMO_X64 test table family.
*   - Does not open the MCC workspace.
* ============================================================

SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64

ECHO ===== X64 MEMO REOPEN CANARY START =====
VERSION

ECHO ===== CLEAN TEST TABLE =====
CLOSE ALL
REL CLEAR ALL
ERASE MEMO_X64 CONFIRM

ECHO ===== CREATE X64 MEMO TABLE =====
CREATE X64 MEMO_X64 (ID N(8,0), TITLE C(20), NOTES M)
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE TITLE WITH X641
REPLACE NOTES WITH "first x64 memo"

ECHO [EXPECT-GREEN] Before close, NOTES should show first x64 memo.
TUP
TUPLE NOTES
STRUCT
FIELDS

ECHO ===== REOPEN READBACK =====
CLOSE
USE MEMO_X64
ECHO [EXPECT-GREEN] After reopen, NOTES should still show first x64 memo.
ECHO [CURRENT-RED] 2026-05-13 observed TUP showing memo reference value 1 instead.
TUP
TUPLE NOTES
STRUCT
FIELDS

ECHO ===== UPDATE AFTER REOPEN =====
ECHO [EXPECT-GREEN] REPLACE NOTES should update memo text after reopen.
ECHO [CURRENT-RED] 2026-05-13 observed: REPLACE: memo backend not attached.
REPLACE NOTES WITH "second x64 memo"
TUP
TUPLE NOTES

ECHO ===== REOPEN SECOND READBACK =====
CLOSE
USE MEMO_X64
ECHO [EXPECT-GREEN] NOTES should show second x64 memo.
TUP
TUPLE NOTES

ECHO ===== CLEAR AFTER REOPEN =====
ECHO [EXPECT-GREEN] Clearing memo field should be accepted.
REPLACE NOTES WITH ""
TUP
TUPLE NOTES

ECHO ===== REINSERT AFTER CLEAR =====
ECHO [EXPECT-GREEN] Reinsert after clear should be accepted and durable.
REPLACE NOTES WITH "third x64 memo after clear"
TUP
TUPLE NOTES

ECHO ===== FINAL REOPEN READBACK =====
CLOSE
USE MEMO_X64
ECHO [EXPECT-GREEN] NOTES should show third x64 memo after clear.
TUP
TUPLE NOTES

ECHO ===== X64 MEMO REOPEN CANARY END =====
CLOSE ALL
